%description:

The BLER lookup has no jump at either end of a curve, and reaches 0 below the
error model's top: BlerCurveErrorModel takes a band above maxSnr() (40 dB) as
error-free without reading the curves, so the curves must be 0 there already.

At its last tabulated point the lookup (GetBLER_TU) fell to 0, where CQI 11 to
15 tabulate an error floor: CQI 11 went from 0.06 at 20 dB to 0 at 21 dB, a
cliff a reception just above it fell off. At the first point of CQI 14 and 15
it jumped to 1, where they tabulate 0.98 and 0.964. The table says nothing
beyond its end points; the model continues each curve's end segment linearly
until it reaches 0 (above the last point) or 1 (below the first), so the
lookup is continuous everywhere and exact at every tabulated point
(BlerCurveTableEnds has the end points themselves).

Checked on every CQI: around each end point, 1 microdB to either side, the
BLER stays within 1e-3 of its value at the point; and the BLER is 0 at 40 dB.

%includes:
#include <cmath>
#include <string>
#include "SchedulerTestUtil.h"
#include "simu5g/common/blerCurves/BLERvsSINR_15CQI_TU.h"

%global:
using namespace simu5g;
using namespace simu5g::unittest;

%activity:
Checker c;
const double eps = 1e-6;
std::string topDetail, bottomDetail, zeroDetail;
for (int cqi = 1; cqi <= 15; cqi++) {
    int row = cqi - 1;
    double first = SINR_15_CQI_TU[row][0], last = SINR_15_CQI_TU[row][15];
    // the BLER just below, at, and just above an end point
    auto around = [&] (double point, std::string& detail) {
        double lo = GetBLER_TU(point - eps, cqi), at = GetBLER_TU(point, cqi), hi = GetBLER_TU(point + eps, cqi);
        if (std::fabs(lo - at) > 1e-3 || std::fabs(hi - at) > 1e-3)
            detail += " cqi" + std::to_string(cqi) + ": " + std::to_string(lo) + ", " + std::to_string(at) + ", " + std::to_string(hi);
    };
    around(last, topDetail);
    around(first, bottomDetail);
    if (GetBLER_TU(40.0, cqi) != 0.0)
        zeroDetail += " cqi" + std::to_string(cqi) + ": " + std::to_string(GetBLER_TU(40.0, cqi));
}
c.check("no curve jumps at its last tabulated point", topDetail.empty(), topDetail);
c.check("no curve jumps at its first tabulated point", bottomDetail.empty(), bottomDetail);
c.check("every curve is 0 at 40 dB, where the error model stops reading the curves", zeroDetail.empty(), zeroDetail);

c.summary();

%contains: stdout
modelchecks=3 modelfailures=0

%not-contains: stdout
FAILED
